    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>This plugin converts JPEG/JPG/PNG to WebP at upload time—before WordPress generates sub-sizes. Supports Imagick (preferred) and GD (fallback). Options for quality, PNG lossless, and delete original.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the folder <code>rs-auto-webp-convert</code> to <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> or upload the zip in WP Admin.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin.</li>\n<li>Go to Settings <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> RS Auto WebP Convert.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.2</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>English readme and strings; fixed Plugin URI vs Author URI.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Automatically converts JPEG/JPG/PNG to WebP on upload, with an option to delete the original. Imagick preferred, GD fallback. No tracking.",
